      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Strategically, while traditional luxury often leverages specific Western aesthetics, modern ultra-premium branding thrives on aspirational fluidity across diverse sophistication. Leaning into established racial tropes can risk alienating newer, highly globalized wealth groups who prefer less prescribed imagery. A more potent approach is to cast individuals who embody *power* and *taste* within the chosen setting, allowing the scent's narrative to borrow prestige from the environment rather than the model's heritage. This allows you to signal an inclusive yet elite echelon of buyers.",
